insert into bev_facts (key, title, body, source, url, as_of, status) values
($tq$mobile-charger$tq$, $tq$Charging without rebuilding the garage$tq$, $tq$Some multi-unit buildings look at a mobile DC charger on an existing power line, instead of a new supply in the underground garage. Designwerk, in Winterthur, makes a mobile DC charger (model 22-920, listed with 21 kW DC output) that plugs into a 3-phase 32 A socket. The maker lists garages, dealerships and fleets as its use, so whether it fits a residential garage is a question for the building. Whether it is allowed depends on that building’s connection and the other owners. It is not a general right, and it is not in the year cost until there is a quote.$tq$, $tq$Designwerk product page for the maker's own description. Project meeting note for the idea. Not confirmed for a residential garage.$tq$, $tq$https://www.designwerk.com/en/mobile-charger-22-920/$tq$, '2026-10-03', $tq$unverified$tq$)
